        },
        "title": "Lionel Validation Study 10",
        "purpose": "Use a tenth specimen as a held-out test of the existing grammar and promote new structure only where the established model genuinely needs refinement.",
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.summary",
          "label": "Lionel Validation Study 10"
        },
        "payload": "node.web.summary",
        "intent": "node",
        "key": "node.web.summary",
        "viewRole": "summary",
        "viewKind": "display",
        "semanticLevel": "summary",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        },
        "markdown": "# Lionel Validation Study 10\n\n## Issue-Sorting Live Monologue\n\nA roughly **1:22:57** live episode moving among the Tyler Robinson prosecution, broader investigative questions, world-order fears, Spain, AI and antique books, everyday cultural life, migration, Trump, coalition realignment, writing, and community.\n\n**Episode family:** `Lionel Live Monologue`  \n**Navigation mode:** `branch-and-return`  \n**Persistent state:** `threadSet`  \n**Major new episode family required:** no\n\n**Strongest discovery:** Lionel explicitly teaches the distinction between related **issues** and repeatedly asks which facts are relevant to which question.\n\n`DEFINE ISSUE RINGS -> STATE PROOF THESIS -> BRANCH -> RETURN TO LEGAL ISSUE -> SORT RELEVANCE -> OPEN NEW THREADS -> RETURN TO ORDER -> MAP COALITION -> REFLECT ON WRITING -> COMMUNITY CLOSE`\n\nThe held-out specimen mostly fits. The important refinement is analytical scope, not another format.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786077619279,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
