        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 📺 Source and Attribution Boundary\n\n**Duration represented:** approximately 1:22:57.\n\nLionel begins in an explicitly didactic mode, saying that a teacher must sometimes repeat the essence of an issue. He distinguishes the question of who killed Charlie Kirk from the narrower question he says a Tyler Robinson trial would decide. \n\nHe then names several separate `rings`: the whodunit, the criminal prosecution, TPUSA and Erica, Candace Owens, and combinations of those questions. \n\nThe transcript contains legal opinions, disputed factual assertions, political claims, speculation, sensitive claims about individuals and groups, and live audience comments. Those remain attributed to Lionel or the quoted audience participant.\n\nThis graph studies rhetorical, analytical, and navigational structure."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study10-central",
      "type": "content",
