        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nStudy 10 makes explicit a distinction the earlier grammar only implied:\n\n## Navigation structure is not analytical structure.\n\nLionel may jump among many threads, but inside each thread he repeatedly asks:\n\n- What question are we answering?\n- What is the governing standard?\n- Which facts bear on that question?\n- Which interesting facts belong to another question?\n\nThe opening `five rings` are therefore more than topics. They are **issue scopes**.\n\nLater Lionel describes this directly as `issue analysis`, asking what the issue, goal, and purpose actually are and warning against importing facts from unrelated disputes. \n\nThis may be the clearest statement yet of Lionel's underlying analytical method."
        }
      }
    },
