        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 3 · World-Order Branch\n## 5:59–14:38\n\nBefore returning to the prosecution, Lionel opens a broad branch about what he calls an orchestrated collapse of order. He develops a Spain and Morocco border story, stresses geography, and treats the event as a warning about borders, authority, and future instability. \n\nHe then asks where people will obtain trustworthy information and calls information itself the new currency. \n\n**Navigation:** a substantial side thread remains conceptually separate from the trial issue."
        }
      }
    },
