        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 4 · Issue Analysis and Proof-Chain Audit\n## 14:38–30:05\n\nLionel returns to the prosecution and explicitly teaches `issue analysis`: arguments fail when people cannot identify the question actually being disputed and instead import unrelated grievances or facts. \n\nHe applies that method to the rifle, arguing that DNA, messages, images, publicity, venue, and other evidence cannot substitute for what he regards as the central forensic link between the alleged weapon and the fatal shot. \n\nHe then uses the recurring lint-brush demonstration to explain a contrasting hypothetical case where direct observation or other physical evidence could make projectile recovery unnecessary. \n\nFinally, he explicitly sorts other allegations back into the `whodunit` ring rather than the prosecution ring. \n\n**Strong recurrence:** evidence audit, proof test, analogy, relevance sorting."
        }
      }
    },
