        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 5 · Multi-Issue Declaration and AI Book Branch\n## 30:05–38:49\n\nLionel pauses and states that citizens must be able to handle many different issues simultaneously. After a brief chat and humor detour, he returns to Spain and then deliberately opens another story. \n\nThe new thread concerns reports that AI companies acquire old books, remove their bindings for scanning, and destroy the physical copies. Lionel treats the story as a loss of human history and material culture rather than merely an AI-training issue. \n\nHe then reconnects AI to the legal thread by imagining AI eventually acting as a juror that would still need to understand reasonable doubt and evidentiary linkage. \n\n**Navigation:** branch, develop independently, then create a semantic bridge back to an earlier issue."
        }
      }
    },
