        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 8 · Trump Disillusionment and Coalition Construction\n## 1:02:24–1:16:05\n\nLionel asks his audience whether anyone still believes Trump is performing at his best, reacts to viewers who say something changed, and again uses the audience as a sampling mechanism rather than simply a source of side chatter. \n\nHe then explicitly constructs a hypothetical new political coalition containing figures such as Candace Owens, Joe Kent, Thomas Massie, MTG, Tulsi Gabbard, and Rand Paul. \n\nThe discussion then distinguishes criticism of Israeli policy or Zionism from suspicion based merely on Jewish identity, and later broadens into a discussion of what government legitimately provides. \n\n**Validation:** actor-field and coalition mapping recur again."
        }
      }
    },
