        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 9 · AI Detection and Writing as Thinking\n## 1:16:05–1:21:10\n\nLionel tells a story about an instructor hiding an absurd instruction inside an essay prompt so that a student who blindly pasted it into ChatGPT would reveal the use of AI. \n\nHe expands from that anecdote into a broader argument about ambiguous writing, love letters, and the relationship between writing and thought. His conclusion is that difficulty writing may reflect failure to understand what one actually thinks. \n\n**Structural role:** return to the episode's deeper epistemic theme: clarity requires identifying and articulating what one actually means."
        }
      }
    },
