          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786077619279,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# ⚖️ Issue Analysis as a Deep Lionel Operation\n\nStudy 10 suggests that several moves we previously treated separately may share one deeper operation:\n\n## `Lionel Performs Issue Analysis`\n\nHe explicitly describes the method as asking:\n\n- What are we talking about?\n- What is the issue?\n- What is the goal?\n- What is the purpose?\n- What really matters?\n- What does not matter to this issue?\n\n\n\nThis may unify or organize:\n\n- Defines Evaluative Standard\n- Separates Analytical Questions\n- Ranks Evidence\n- Returns to Omitted Evidence\n- Audits Evidence\n- Reenacts Proof Test\n- Rejects Irrelevant Detail\n\nThe repeated legal examples are implementations of a more general **scope-and-relevance discipline**."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study10-navigation",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Navigation and Relevance Are Orthogonal",
