        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786077619279,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 🧵 Navigation and Relevance Are Orthogonal\n\nStudy 08 established a set of persistent storylines.\n\nStudy 10 shows why the graph must not confuse that navigation state with analytical relevance.\n\nA discussion can move:\n\n`trial -> Spain -> trial -> AI books -> pizza -> migration -> Trump -> writing`\n\nwhile the trial evidence itself remains organized under a much narrower issue scope.\n\nTherefore Twilite should be able to represent both:\n\n## Conversation topology\n- thread set\n- active thread\n- branch\n- return point\n\n## Argument topology\n- issue scope\n- claim\n- standard\n- evidence\n- relevance relationship\n\nThe two graphs overlap, but they are not the same graph."
        }
      }
    },
