        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 📏 Confidence and Design Implication\n\n## High confidence\n- no new episode family is needed\n- branch-and-return and thread-set navigation recur\n- issue analysis is a stable Lionel behavior\n- legal proof audits are applications of a broader scope-and-relevance method\n- topic navigation and argument relevance must be modeled separately\n- coalition mapping continues to recur\n- audience input remains multi-role\n- the ontology is strongly converging\n\n## Medium confidence\n- `Issue Scope` should become an explicit shared node class rather than a property on Topic\n- `Lionel Performs Issue Analysis` deserves a permanent show-specific class\n- the five-ring model should be represented as several Issue Scope nodes rather than one container node\n\n## Design implication\nTen specimens appear sufficient to begin a **first production grammar draft**.\n\nFurther transcripts are still useful for validation, but the next high-value task is no longer unconstrained discovery. It is to design the reusable class set, model a fresh episode with those classes, and see where the actual authoring experience breaks."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
